The main change is to call the virtual `GetType()` once and keep the result in a local, instead of calling it twice. This assumes `GetType()` returns the same value on repeated calls, which holds for the SDK's field types.

The second change avoids an integer divide in the common cases. Base-type sizes are normally 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes, and those divisions become a plain read or a shift. Any other size still uses ordinary division, so results are identical for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
    {
        const size_t n = values.size();
        const FIT_UINT8 sz = baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK];
        switch (sz)
        {
        case 1: return (FIT_UINT8)n;
        case 2: return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 1);
        case 4: return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 2);
        case 8: return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 3);
        default: return (FIT_UINT8)(n / sz);
        }
    }

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```